I have a few suggestions for things to add to NH:
-Another intrinsic, paralysis resistance. This would protect from potions of
paralysis, floating eyes, etc. You could get it with a ring of paralysis 
resistance, or by eating the right monster...
-A ring of vampiric regeneration. While wearing it, you would get half of the
HP of physical damage you inflicted to other people added to your HPs
-A floating disc which follows you around and carries items for you. It would
reduce your burden, but monsters could grab stuff off of it. It would follow
you like a ball and chain...
-You should be able to pay shopkeepers of the appropriate type to identify
your items for you. So you could chat with a antique weapons dealer and he
would (for half what it would cost to sell to you) identify any weapons you
were carrying
-A wand of security. When you zap it creates a extradimensional pocket
in which you can hang around and heal yourself (and get hungry :( ) for as
long as you want befor exiting to the real world at exactly the time you left.
-A ring of increase levels. It could be +1 to +5. It works just like a ring
of increase strength, but it temporarily grants you extra levels (speaking
of which, does your level affect your chance to hit and/or you chance to
learn spells?)
-Boots of kicking: While you wear these you get two attacks (your normal attack
and a kick) whenever you attack something, just like all the monsters that
get multiple attacks
-Wishes should be more powerful. Instead of just giving you an item, it should
say something like: You get to make a wish. Would you like to:
1)Summon an item
2)Give yourself an intrinsic ability
3)Raise one of your statistics to 20
4)Gain 5 levels of experience
...
etc.
-It should be possible to increase the plus on things like rings of protection
and rings of increase damage by wielding them and reading scrolls of enchant
weapon
-There should be a command which tells you where the ladders on a level are,
if you've found them. It's really annoying when the ladder is under an item,
and you have to wander throughout the entire level looking for it under 
everything
-Get rid of rust traps. Or change them so that it says "your armor is hit by
a gush of water" and then you have to take your armor off and dry it off or
it will get rusty. The way they are right now is just such a pisser!
-Corpses should stay fresh for longer. This is especially annoying when you
kill something and you pick it up and carry it two rooms over to the shrine
so you can #offer it and its _already_ rotten. Grr!
-There should be rings of chaos. Every time you put it on, it function as a
different ring, but unless its an obvious one (like levitation or
invisibility) you can't tell what it is.
-There should be some physical item (like an oilcan) which will remove
the rust from things... (but not make them rustproof)
-There should be some item (such as cotton balls) which you can stick in
your ears. It will keep you from hearing anything, but if you stick cotton
in your ears and blindfold yourself, you should be unable to see or hear
nymphs so they couldn't seduce you.
-It would be nice if you could get a general idea of how damaged monsters were
when you hit them, ie "You hit the giant beetle. The giant beetle is seriously
wounded."
-If you have a screen of more than 25 lines (which most people do) it should
be possible to use more than one line for messages (to avoid all those damn
--more-- 's)
-Another neat items would be flasks of greek fire. You could throw them, and
wherever they hit something they would stop and create an explosion (a la 
scroll of fire)
-If you dip a weapon into a blessed potion and then immediately read a scroll
of enchant weapon, the weapon should gain the ability of the potion. For
instance, you could get a long sword of paralysis or a spear of blindness.
(This shouldn't work for potions of gain ability or gain experience.)
Even better, there could be a very special (and rare) item called a potion of
enchantment. (It would have to be about as rare as spellbooks of finger of
death.... finding more than one or two per game would make it boring instead
of neat.). Any magical item could be dissolved in a potion of enchantment. The
potion would then take on its property. Any weapon or armor could then be 
dipped into the potion and take on that property. If the potion of enchantment
was blessed, and if a blessed scroll of enchant armor/weapon were then 
immediately read, the property would become permanent. So you could make
yourself a long sword of fire, a helmet of light, a shield of conflict, a
spear of death, etc.
-It should be possible to overload wands (like phasers on Star Trek). Doing so
would use all the charges and destroy the wand (and would require > 75% of
the charges left to work) but would create an extremely powerful magical effect
of the type of the wand. For instance, overloading a wand of fire would give
a room-filling fireball, overloading a wand of light would give a bright flash
that blinded all creatures in sight, and also lit the entire level. Etc.

Well, that's enough for now


